{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group C of the [[2002 FIFA World Cup]]''' took place between 3 and 13 June 2002. The group consisted of eventual champions [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], [[Turkey national football team|Turkey]], [[Costa Rica national football team|Costa Rica]], and [[China national football team|China]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Manaschev |first=Erlan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2002full.html |title=World Cup 2002 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=3 July 2008 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> Brazil finished top of the group, winning all three matches, and advanced to the second round, alongside Turkey. Costa Rica were eliminated on goal difference, having shared the same number of points as Turkey, while China lost all three of their matches, failing to score a goal in any of them.

